cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Admissible-Pooling: Interval Max-Pooling with Admissible Orders for Certified Robustness"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MohammadMahdi-Sharifbeigy/admissible-pooling"
url: "https://github.com/MohammadMahdi-Sharifbeigy/admissible-pooling"
abstract: >
  Code accompanying the paper "Which Admissible Orders Make Interval Max-Pooling
  Inclusion-Preserving? A Characterization for Interval-Valued Convolutional Networks"
  (submitted to Fuzzy Sets and Systems). The repository provides a PyTorch implementation
  of sound and unsound interval max-pooling operators (Lattice, Lex2, Lex1, Xu–Yager)
  together with certified-training pipelines for CNN and GNN benchmarks.
